# Copy to .env; the Makefile reads it when present. This file is committed: every
# value is a development default or a placeholder, never a real secret.

# Database. goen connects and immediately does SET ROLE store, so the schema's
# privilege model applies to the running binary; it refuses to serve if the
# session is still a superuser after that.
GOEN_DATABASE_URL=postgres://goen:goen@127.0.0.1:5433/goen?sslmode=disable

# The back office does SET ROLE admin. Defaults to GOEN_DATABASE_URL, which is
# right in development (the owning superuser can assume any role) and wrong
# elsewhere: point it at admin_svc so a storefront connection is not also the
# back office.
# GOEN_ADMIN_DATABASE_URL=postgres://admin_svc:changeme@db.internal:5432/goen?sslmode=verify-full

# The recommendation worker, as maintenance_svc. Startup pings this pool, so a
# login that cannot SET ROLE maintenance fails before the server listens.
# GOEN_MAINTENANCE_DATABASE_URL=postgres://maintenance_svc:changeme@db.internal:5432/goen?sslmode=verify-full

# Outside development, point each URL at its _svc role (NOSUPERUSER, owns
# nothing, so RESET ROLE cannot escalate) and run migrations as goen on a
# separate connection. A superuser login makes goen log a warning.

GOEN_ADDR=127.0.0.1:9700
GOEN_LOG_LEVEL=info

# The origin Stripe returns the customer to and every emailed link points at.
# Credentials, a path, query or fragment are refused; with Secure cookies it must
# be https, because reset and verification URLs carry single-use tokens. The
# http:// + GOEN_ADDR fallback is development only.
# GOEN_BASE_URL=https://goen.example

# Development only; `make run` sets it. A Secure, __Host- cookie never returns
# over http://, so the cart would lose itself. The default is secure, so
# forgetting this in a deployment fails safe.
# GOEN_INSECURE_COOKIES=1

# Stripe. Prefer a restricted key (rk_). With no key the payment page says
# payments are off and nothing else changes. A key without a webhook secret
# refuses to start: it would take money over an unauthenticated endpoint.
# GOEN_STRIPE_API_KEY=rk_test_replace_me
# GOEN_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_replace_me

# 統一發票 (ECPay). With no credentials goen issues nothing and says so; half a
# configuration refuses to start. These are ECPay's published staging
# credentials, usable without a contract, and they file into a shared sandbox:
# never use them anywhere real. Going live changes these three values and
# GOEN_ECPAY_BASE_URL.
# GOEN_ECPAY_MERCHANT_ID=2000132
# GOEN_ECPAY_HASH_KEY=ejCk326UnaZWKisg
# GOEN_ECPAY_HASH_IV=q9jcZX8Ib9LM8wYk
# Defaults to https://einvoice-stage.ecpay.com.tw; production is
# https://einvoice.ecpay.com.tw.
# GOEN_ECPAY_BASE_URL=

# 超商取貨 store map (ECPay logistics). Unset removes store pickup everywhere:
# c2c (店到店) or b2c (大宗寄倉), whichever contract ECPay approved. It reuses
# GOEN_ECPAY_MERCHANT_ID and has no key or IV, because the map endpoint signs
# nothing; the returned store is checked against a nonce this browser holds.
# Staging shares id 2000132 with the invoice sandbox, so development uses b2c,
# and ECPay's staging answers with one fixed store and no map by design.
# GOEN_ECPAY_LOGISTICS=b2c
# Defaults to https://logistics-stage.ecpay.com.tw, and to
# https://logistics.ecpay.com.tw when GOEN_STRIPE_API_KEY is a live key.
# GOEN_ECPAY_LOGISTICS_BASE_URL=

# Google sign-in. With no credentials the button is absent and its two routes
# 404. Both or neither. Add GOEN_BASE_URL + /auth/google/callback as the OAuth
# client's authorised redirect URI.
# GOEN_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=replace_me.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOEN_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=replace_me

# Public demonstration only. With both set, every start makes this address a
# verified customer with this password, the sign-in page prints both, and the
# account cannot change itself because every visitor shares it. Both or neither,
# and neither beside a live GOEN_STRIPE_API_KEY.
# GOEN_DEMO_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=demo@goen.example
# GOEN_DEMO_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD=replace_me

# Staff second factor: 32 random bytes, hex or base64 (`openssl rand -hex 32`).
# It is a key, not a passphrase; goen refuses anything that does not decode to 32
# bytes. It encrypts stored TOTP secrets, so a database dump alone cannot defeat
# the second factor.
# CHANGING IT makes every enrolled credential unreadable: remove each factor at
# /admin/staff while the old binary runs, restart with the new key and have staff
# re-enrol. If /admin is already unreachable, run
# `DELETE FROM staff_totp_credentials;` as the owning role first.
# Empty disables enrolment, but it is required once GOEN_INSECURE_COOKIES is
# unset: without it the back office falls back to a password alone, so goen
# refuses to start.
# GOEN_TOTP_KEY=replace_me

# CIDRs whose X-Forwarded-For goen believes, comma-separated. Empty believes
# nobody and keys every rate limit on the connection's address. Set it if
# anything terminates TLS in front of goen, or every visitor shares the proxy's
# bucket and one attacker can exhaust sign-in for all.
# List the address the proxy connects from: a same-host proxy reaches a loopback
# listener from 127.0.0.1 or ::1. goen refuses to start when the list names no
# address that can reach a loopback GOEN_ADDR, and refuses 0.0.0.0/0, which
# lets any client choose its own rate-limit key.
# GOEN_TRUSTED_PROXIES=127.0.0.1,::1

# Mail. With no address, development logs mail and the outbox marks it
# delivered, which would silently lose password resets and receipts in
# production, so a production posture requires an address. A configured relay
# whose address is not host:port is fatal rather than falling back to the log.
# GOEN_SMTP_ADDR=smtp.example:587
# GOEN_SMTP_FROM=goen <no-reply@goen.example>
# GOEN_SMTP_USER=
# GOEN_SMTP_PASSWORD=

# Seller (消保法 §18): name and contact the consumer can reach. Order mail
# carries the disclosure only when both are set; otherwise goen logs a warning at
# startup. Set both before taking real orders.
# GOEN_SELLER=Example Shop Ltd.
# GOEN_SELLER_CONTACT=support@goen.example

# A Stripe key that is not a test key (sk_live_, rk_live_ or any unrecognised
# form) refuses to start beside any staging or placeholder setting: partial
# ECPay invoice credentials, an empty or staging GOEN_ECPAY_BASE_URL, a staging
# GOEN_ECPAY_LOGISTICS_BASE_URL, a GOEN_SMTP_FROM that is unparsable or on
# goen.example, a demo account, or insecure cookies. A test key (sk_test_,
# rk_test_, rkcs_test_) or no key is sandbox and refuses nothing new. These
# checks do not authenticate credentials.
